▸ Thought for 6s

  I have drafted and published the comprehensive Technical
  Requirements Document in the project root: TRD.md.
  Here is an architectural summary of the plan:
  ──────
  ### 1. Presentation Structure (6 Tactical Modules)

  • Slide 1: The Multi-Layered Shield (Strategic Doctrine & Threat
  Spectrum)
      • Focus: Reaction time constraints, asymmetric warfare, and
      altitude vs. range threat spectrum (mortars to hypersonic
      MRBMs).
      • Interactive Component: Threat Classifier & Radar Sweep,
      dynamically revealing velocity, detection windows, and tier
      assignment.
  • Slide 2: Tier 1 – Iron Dome (C-RAM, UAVs & Tactical Rockets)
      • Focus: EL/M-2084 AESA radar, Tamir interceptor, and the
      economic Predicted Impact Point (PIP) selective algorithm.
      • Interactive Component: Live Iron Dome Intercept Simulator
      (toggle multi-rocket salvo, selective open-field vs. urban
      intercept logic).
  • Slide 3: Tier 2 – David’s Sling (Medium-to-Long Range & Cruise
  Missiles)
      • Focus: Heavy artillery rockets, low-flying cruise missiles,
      and the Stunner asymmetric "dolphin nose" dual RF/IIR seeker.
      • Interactive Component: Dual-Seeker Evasion & Lock-On
      Simulator (toggle electronic jamming/chaff to demonstrate
      sensor fusion).
  • Slide 4: Tiers 3 & 4 – Arrow 2 & Arrow 3 (Upper & Exo-
  Atmospheric Defense)
      • Focus: Super Green Pine radar, high-altitude atmospheric
      intercept (Arrow 2), and exo-atmospheric hit-to-kill kinetic
      space interception (Arrow 3).
      • Interactive Component: Exo-Atmospheric Apogee & Staging
      Visualizer (interactive altitude slider from Sea Level to Low
      Earth Orbit).
  • Slide 5: Integrated C4I Multi-Tier Command Matrix & Iron Beam
      • Focus: Unified sensor-to-shooter data links, Battle
      Management Center (BMC) multi-tier allocation, and Iron Beam
      laser cost-asymmetry.
      • Interactive Component: Unified Air Defense Director Mini-
      Scenario (simultaneous multi-threat encounter with automated
      vs. manual tier assignment).
  • Slide 6: Strategic Takeaways, Global Impact & Academic Synthesis
      • Focus: International adoption (Arrow 3 in Germany / David's
      Sling in Finland), Home Front Command early warning
      integration, and future hypersonic frontiers.
      • Interactive Component: Filterable Multi-Tier Technical
      Comparison Matrix and Collapsible Academic Bibliography &
      Reference Drawer.
  ──────
  ### 2. 3D Component: Three.js Tactical Defense Hemisphere

  • Persistent WebGL Scene: Semicircular geodesic domes representing
  real-world operational envelopes (Iron Dome in green, David's
  Sling in amber, Arrow in electric cyan).
  • Interactive Controls: Mouse orbit/zoom controls with preset
  perspective toggles (Tactical Overlook, Iron Dome Horizon, Arrow 3
  Orbital View).
  • Dynamic Intercept Vectors: 3D Catmull-Rom ballistic trajectory
  curves with glowing particle trails and kinetic impact burst
  effects.
  ──────
  ### 3. "Aegis Command UI" Design System

  • Palette: Deep Space Navy (#06090e), Surface Glass (rgba(12, 18,
  29, 0.75)), Tactical Cyan (#00f0ff), Emerald Kill Confirmation
  (#00ff88), Threat Alert Crimson (#ff2a55), Warning Amber (#ffb700).
  • Visual Styling: Coordinate grids, subtle radar scanlines,
  glassmorphic HUD telemetry cards, and aerospace corner brackets.
  • Typography: Rajdhani / Chakra Petch display headers paired with
  Space Mono / Consolas telemetry readouts.
  ──────
  ### 4. Incremental Git Release Strategy
  • Milestone 0 (m0-scaffold): Semantic HTML5 shell, Three.js vendor
  setup, base state controller.
  • Milestone 1 (m1-design-system): CSS design tokens, tactical HUD
  layout, keyboard/touch slide navigation FSM.
  • Milestone 2 (m2-threejs-engine): Interactive Three.js 3D defense
  domes, trajectory engine, and camera presets.
  • Milestone 3 (m3-defense-tiers): Dedicated interactive
  simulations for Slides 2, 3, and 4 (Iron Dome, David's Sling,
  Arrow 3).
  • Milestone 4 (m4-c4i-matrix): Multi-threat C4I decision console
  and sensor-to-shooter allocation simulator (Slide 5).
  • Milestone 5 (m5-release-v1): Comparison matrix, academic
  bibliography modal, audio telemetry FX (muted by default), offline
  build verification.
  ──────
  Please review the detailed requirements in TRD.md.

  Do you approve this technical plan, or would you like to adjust
  any slides, interactive simulations, or technical constraints
  before we begin Milestone 0?

